格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh-minato — 社区版本机部署运维套件 for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): install / start / monitor, backup & restore, diagnose and quarantine broken plugins (unofficial) · 安装 / 启动监控 / 备份恢复 / 插件诊断与隔离","id":"gh:1335025041","install_available":true,"language":"C#","name":"dsh-minato","slug":"sakanamaru/dsh-minato","topics":["avalonia","backup","checksum-verification","cli","cordis","cross-platform","csharp","data-integrity","deepseek","deepseek-harness","diagnostics","dotnet","dsh","dsh-plugin","gui","linux","plugin","troubleshooting","unofficial","windows-tool"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh-minato — 社区版本机部署运维套件 for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): install / start / monitor, backup & restore, di"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"agnose and quarantine broken plugins (unofficial) · 安装 / 启动监控 / 备份恢复 / 插件诊断与隔离"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DeepSeek Harness Toolkit — `dsh-minato`"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A no-terminal-needed installer, monitor, backup and repair toolbox for DeepSeek Harness (dsh).**\nW"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"indows and Linux. Runs locally. No telemetry, no accounts, no uploads."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Unofficial.** This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to DeepSeek. It "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"is a third-party\n> helper that drives the `dsh` command line you already have.\n>\n> **English** · 简体中"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ird-party\n> helper that drives the `dsh` command line you already have.\n>\n> **English** · 简体中文 · 日本語"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Everything below is the real interface, captured against a **fixture data directory** — no real sess"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ion, path or\nfigure appears in these images."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| Dashboard | Sessions & tokens | Backup |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Health check | Settings | Update centre |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The remaining pages (overview, plugins, about, logs) and the CLI"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Overview | Plugins | About | Logs |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| CLI menu | CLI status |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"`dsh` is a command-line tool. Installing it, starting it, backing it up and working out why it will "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"not boot are all\nterminal jobs — and the Web UI itself has no entry point for any of them."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"This toolkit puts those jobs behind a window you can double-click:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"- **No terminal needed** — install, start, stop, update and uninstall from a GUI.\n- **A backup you c"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"an trust** — packages carry a completion marker and a content hash, so a truncated one is refused\nin"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"stead of silently restored.\n- **A straight answer when something breaks** — the health check names t"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"he failing piece and prints the one line\nthat fixes it, instead of leaving you with a stack trace."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| **Install dsh** | Double-click. No terminal, no Node.js knowledge required. It installs the CLI, s"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ets up the PATH and Start-menu entry, and keeps an uninstaller beside the install. |\n| **Start / sto"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"p / monitor** | One button for the Web UI, with a live status line and the URL to open. |\n| **Back u"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"p and restore** | Sessions, settings and credentials — packaged with a completion marker and a conte"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"nt hash so a truncated or tampered package is refused rather than restored. |\n| **Backup manager** |"},{"id":"p17s6","text":" See exactly what each package contains before you touch it. |\n| **Migrate to another PC** | Export "},{"id":"p17s7","text":"a package, import it on the new machine. |\n| **Update centre** | One place for the web UI, the offic"},{"id":"p17s8","text":"ial desktop app, this tool, and installed plugins. |\n| **Health check** | \"What exactly is broken?\" "},{"id":"p17s9","text":"— it names the failing piece and prints the one line that fixes it. |\n| **Uninstall** | **Never dele"},{"id":"p17s10","text":"tes your data by default**, and refuses to delete a directory that does not look like an install. |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Windows"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Download `dsh-minato-<version>-win-x64-setup.exe` from Releases and run it."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- The Windows binaries are **not digitally signed**, so SmartScreen may show an \"unknown publisher\" "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"prompt the first\ntime. Verify the download against the published `.sha256` (and the GPG-signed `hash"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"es.txt`) before running it.\n- Prefer a portable copy? Use `dsh-minato-win-x64.zip`, unzip, and run `"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"nning it.\n- Prefer a portable copy? Use `dsh-minato-win-x64.zip`, unzip, and run `gui\\dsht-gui.exe`."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Linux"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Download `dsh-minato-linux-x64.tar.gz`, then:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Uninstall with `./install.sh --uninstall` (add `--force` only if you have moved the installation you"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ll with `./install.sh --uninstall` (add `--force` only if you have moved the installation yourself)."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"1. Install (above) and open **dsh-minato**.\n2. The dashboard shows the current state. If `dsh` is mi"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ssing, the health check says so and offers the fix.\n3. Press **Start** and open the Web UI URL it pr"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ints.\n4. Before you change anything, press **Backup**."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## The GUI"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Ten pages, all reachable from the left rail:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Page | What it is for |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| **Overview** | One screen: what is installed, what is running, what is out of date. |\n| **Dashboar"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"d** | Key figures — sessions, cache-hit rate, tokens — and one-click start/stop. |\n| **Sessions & to"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"kens** | Per-session breakdown, parent/child grouping, sortable. |\n| **Plugins** | Which plugins a p"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"rofile has, which are disabled, and which would break a boot. |\n| **Backup** | Create, inspect, veri"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"fy, restore, export and delete packages. |\n| **Health check** | The \"what is broken\" report, with th"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"e exact prescription. Run it when you want it — it does not run by itself. |\n| **Settings** | Langua"},{"id":"p31s7","text":"ge, port, behaviour — without editing YAML. |\n| **About** | Version, credits, and what this tool del"},{"id":"p31s8","text":"iberately does not do. |\n| **Update centre** | Update dsh, the desktop app, this tool or a plugin. |"},{"id":"p31s9","text":"\n| **Logs** | Filter, search and export the launcher log. |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Safety and privacy — what is actually true"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"This section states only what the code does. If a claim here is not backed by the code, it is a bug;"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"s only what the code does. If a claim here is not backed by the code, it is a bug; please report it."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"- **Local only.** The tool reads and writes your own machine. It contacts the network **only** in th"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ese commands:\n`check`, `update-info`, `update-center`, `doctor`, `install`, `update`, `verify-instal"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"l --url`, and `balance` (only\nwhen you have set `balance_key` in settings; without it the command is"},{"id":"p34s4","text":" fully offline). Everything else — status,\nsessions, cost, backup, restore, logs — never opens a con"},{"id":"p34s5","text":"nection.\n- **No telemetry, no accounts, no uploads.**\n- **Your data is not deleted by uninstall.** U"},{"id":"p34s6","text":"ninstall removes the tool's own files. Data removal is a separate,\nexplicit action.\n- **Backup integ"},{"id":"p34s7","text":"rity is checked, not assumed.** A package carries a completion marker written last and a per-file\nha"},{"id":"p34s8","text":"sh; a package that was interrupted, or whose contents changed, is refused.\n- **Zero third-party runt"},{"id":"p34s9","text":"ime dependencies** for the CLI, the installer, the launcher and the dsh plugin. The GUI is\nbuilt on "},{"id":"p34s10","text":"Avalonia (a UI framework), which is the one exception.\n- **Your API key, if you set one, is stored i"},{"id":"p34s11","text":"n plain text** in your local config file and is only ever sent to the\nDeepSeek API endpoint by the `"},{"id":"p34s12","text":"balance` command. Leave it empty and nothing is stored."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
